description:
Company Background

 Our client is a global leader in advanced energy storage solutions, specializing in the design and manufacturing of automotive batteries. Headquartered in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, the company serves major automakers and aftermarket retailers, producing over 150 million batteries annually and powering 1 in 3 vehicles worldwide. With operations in more than 50 countries, the company focuses on innovative and sustainable battery technologies for conventional, hybrid, and electric vehicles, supporting the evolving mobility ecosystem.

 Project Description

 The project focuses on consolidating existing SMS and email prototypes into a single production-ready solution with a user interface for scheduling, configuration, monitoring, and logging. The solution is being built using Power Apps within the company’s environment, with integrations to Snowflake and existing Python and SQL logic.

 Technologies


 Power Apps (UI, workflows, SharePoint integrations)

 Azure Functions (API endpoints, data processing)

 Python scripting

 SQL

 Snowflake


 What You'll Do


 Migrate the existing messaging solution from Python to Power Apps;

 Enhance and optimize the current SMS solution based on the new messaging architecture;

 Ensure performance, scalability, and reliability of the solution;

 Implement and support global HDIR file upload functionality;

 Design and develop API endpoints for Generic Customer APIs;

 Communicate directly with the client as the primary point of contact for the project;


 Job Requirements


 5+ years of experience as a Data Engineer;

 Hands-on experience with SQL and Snowflake;

 Experience working with high-load systems and data processing optimization;

 Strong understanding of Microsoft Power Apps for UI development, workflow implementation, and SharePoint integrations;

 Experience with Azure Functions, including building API endpoints and implementing compute-intensive processing;

 Understanding of Python scripting;

 Familiarity with security best practices, including encryption, secure data handling, and compliance with industry regulations;

 Experience with Power Apps is a plus;

 Self-motivated, resourceful, and able to work effectively with minimal guidance in a dynamic environment;

 Ability to adapt quickly and work effectively in Agile or iterative delivery teams;

 Strong written and verbal communication skills in English;


 What Do We Offer

 The global benefits package includes:


 Technical and non-technical training for professional and personal growth;

 Internal conferences and meetups to learn from industry experts;

 Support and mentorship from an experienced employee to help you professional grow and development;

 Health insurance;

 Sports activities to promote a healthy lifestyle;

 Flexible work options, including remote and hybrid opportunities;

 Referral program for bringing in new talent;

 Work anniversary program and additional vacation days.
